tweets.text:
Anthropic just filed to go public.

The ticker will be ANT, and the hosts say they're aiming to raise $100 billion.

The same week, Google lost about $500 billion in value in a single day.

I pulled the biggest moments from this week's @theallinpod and added my own take.

@DavidSacks explains the $80 billion "loss" and why he calls Anthropic a model of capital efficiency.

@friedberg walks through how fast big customers are growing.

@chamath digs into the risk factors and asks if AI borrowing could crowd out Treasuries.

@Jason on Google's wild week.

As someone who relies on AI every day, this one hit home for me.

Commentary is in my own voice, cloned with AI.

Watch and tell me what you think.

